These are the omarchy68k screen savers, written for A/UX on the
Macintosh SE/30: the ten 68k
assembly engines (decrypt.s, storm.s, extras.s, motion.s), the glyph
stamper (raster.s), the effect table (effects.c), the self-test
(effects-test.c), the banner and the font. They are copied unchanged
except for the banner's bottom line, which names se30os instead of
A/UX 3.1.1. Their licences and attributions are in LICENSE, NOTICE and
BRANDING-LICENSE.

se30os runs them the way the A/UX direct demo did, stamping glyphs
straight into video RAM; the driver is src/saver.c. compat/ holds the
two libc headers the C files include.
